<!--
Cooling device order for CPU on MacBookPro11,4.

rapl_controller is deliberately REMOVED from this list: the package power
limits (PL2 60W / PL1 37W) are owned by intel-undervolt, and thermald was
resetting PL1 back to the firmware value of 100W whenever temps dropped.
intel_powerclamp is also excluded; its idle injection caused cursor lag on
this machine and the module is blacklisted. thermald therefore cools by
capping frequency, which is the intended behaviour here.

NOTE: do not write a double hyphen anywhere inside this comment. XML forbids
it, libxml2 rejects the whole file, and thermald then silently falls back to
its built-in order with rapl_controller first. That happened on 2026-07-25.
-->

<CoolingDeviceOrder>
	<CoolingDevice>intel_pstate</CoolingDevice>
	<CoolingDevice>cpufreq</CoolingDevice>
	<CoolingDevice>Processor</CoolingDevice>
</CoolingDeviceOrder>
